# /etc/talyvor/bff.env — the BFF's entire runtime surface.
#   chown root:talyvor /etc/talyvor/bff.env && chmod 640 /etc/talyvor/bff.env
# (0640, not 0600: systemd reads this as root, but the preflight boot — and any
# as-talyvor debugging — sources it AS THE SERVICE USER; group-read makes that
# possible while everyone else is kept out. See deploy/README.md §4.)
# Every value here is documented, with its failure mode, in deploy/README.md §4.
# The BFF fails closed: a missing required value refuses to start and names itself.

# ── Bind & mode ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 0.0.0.0, NOT loopback, on this server: Caddy is a CONTAINER (the Lens stack's
# compose), and from inside it 127.0.0.1 is the container — it reaches the host
# only over the Docker bridge, so a loopback-bound BFF is unreachable ("dial
# tcp 172.17.0.1:8787: i/o timeout"). The bind guard permits this ONLY because
# BFF_AUTH_MODE=oidc with an https BFF_PUBLIC_BASE_URL; ufw scopes :8787 to the
# bridge range (172.16.0.0/12 — README §3a). For loopback dev, 127.0.0.1:8787.
BFF_ADDR=0.0.0.0:8787
# Production posture. ("disabled" is the loopback-only dev mode.)
BFF_AUTH_MODE=oidc

# ── Web bundle ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where the built SPA lives on the server. REQUIRED here in practice: the
# compiled-in default (../web/dist) is a repo-relative dev path that means
# nothing under systemd, and the unit deliberately does not set it.
WEB_DIST=/opt/talyvor/web-dist

# ── OIDC (all five required in oidc mode) ────────────────────────────────────
# The browser-facing origin. Bare origin, https, no path — it derives the
# redirect URI (<origin>/auth/callback) and scopes the __Host- session cookie.
BFF_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://app.talyvor.com
# The issuer. Google (recommended for the trial): https://accounts.google.com
# The BFF discovers it at boot; the BROWSER must be able to reach it too.
OIDC_ISSUER=https://accounts.google.com
# The confidential client registered at the IdP, with redirect URI EXACTLY
# https://app.talyvor.com/auth/callback
OIDC_CLIENT_ID=REPLACE_ME.apps.googleusercontent.com
OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=REPLACE_ME
# Comma-separated trial allowlist (matched lower-cased against the id_token
# email; unverified emails are refused). "*" alone = any issuer identity.
OIDC_ALLOWED_EMAILS=you@example.com,teammate@example.com
# Optional; default 12h. Sessions are in-memory: a BFF restart signs everyone out.
#BFF_SESSION_TTL=12h

# ── Lens (both required, always) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# https for a remote Lens box — ENFORCED at boot (a bearer credential rides every
# request to it; http is allowed only on loopback, for dev).
LENS_BASE_URL=https://REPLACE_ME_LENS_HOST
#
# ⚠ PER-USER PROVISIONING (suite #30). LENS_WORKSPACE_KEY and LENS_WORKSPACE_ID
# ARE NO LONGER READ — every signed-in person is provisioned their OWN Lens
# workspace at login, and each request carries that session's own token. Leaving
# the old variables in the file is harmless (nothing reads them) but misleading;
# delete them. What is required instead:
#
#   LENS_PROVISION_SECRET — gates Lens's POST /v1/provision. It must be the SAME
#   VALUE Lens itself boots with (LENS_PROVISION_SECRET in the lens stack). One
#   value, two places, like the Track/Docs gateway secrets below.
#
#   Unset here  ⇒ the BFF REFUSES TO START ("LENS_PROVISION_SECRET is required").
#   Unset on Lens ⇒ Lens does not register the route at all, so provisioning 404s
#                   and EVERY LOGIN FAILS (the BFF hard-stops rather than falling
#                   back to a shared workspace). Both sides, or neither.
LENS_PROVISION_SECRET=REPLACE_ME
#
# ⚠ LENS_API_KEY MUST NOT BE SET HERE. The BFF refuses to boot if it is present.
# The Lens admin key authorises EVERY workspace and ~30 admin routes; the
# provisioning secret can only create a workspace and mint its session token. If
# you are tempted to set it because "provisioning needs privileges" — it does
# not, and the refusal is deliberate.

# ── Track (optional trio: all three or none; oidc mode only) ─────────────────
# Unset ⇒ /api/track/* and /api/members answer 503; the rest of the app works.
# Trial users must also be MEMBERS of this workspace (X-User-Email is the join key).
#
# BASE URL — 127.0.0.1, NOT a docker service name. The BFF is a HOST process
# (talyvor-bff.service), so it does not use Docker's resolver, and its own config
# check refuses anything that is neither https nor loopback: `http://track:3000`
# fails boot with "must be https (http is allowed only on loopback, for dev)".
# The Track container publishes 127.0.0.1:3000 (deploy/track-docs.compose.yaml).
#
# THE SECRET IS ONE VALUE UNDER TWO NAMES. TRACK_GATEWAY_SECRET here must equal
# the GATEWAY_AUTH_SECRET Track itself boots with. Get this wrong and nothing
# crashes: Track's gatewayauth middleware 401s BEFORE reading any identity
# header, so /api/track/* fails while every other screen keeps working — a
# half-deploy that looks like a Track bug. deploy/README.md §"Deploying Track
# and Docs" generates both from one command for exactly this reason.
#TRACK_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3000
#TRACK_GATEWAY_SECRET=
#TRACK_WORKSPACE_ID=

# ── Docs (optional trio: all three or none; oidc mode only) ──────────────────
# Unset ⇒ /api/docs/* answers 503. Same loopback rule and same
# one-value-two-names rule as Track above.
#
# DOCS_WORKSPACE_ID must equal the container's DOCS_DEFAULT_WORKSPACE: the BFF
# pins its upstream path to /v1/workspaces/<id>/spaces, so a mismatch is a 404
# on a workspace that exists.
#
# The Docs secret additionally may NEVER be the published placeholder
# "dev-only-insecure-gateway-secret-change-me" — Docs rejects it forever,
# regardless of length, because it is in git history and therefore public.
#DOCS_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4000
#DOCS_GATEWAY_SECRET=
#DOCS_WORKSPACE_ID=default
